"""
Problem:
--------
Given two integers left and right, return the bitwise AND of every number
between left and right (inclusive).

Example:
    Input:  left = 5, right = 7

    5 = 101
    6 = 110
    7 = 111

    101 & 110 & 111 = 100

    Output: 4

Key Idea:
---------
We only keep the bits that remain unchanged throughout the range.

The trick:
    right & (right - 1)

This removes the lowest set bit (rightmost 1-bit).

Keep doing this until right == left.
The remaining value contains the common prefix bits.

Why it works:
-------------
Any bit that changes somewhere between left and right
cannot be 1 in the final AND.

So we remove those changing set bits from right until
both numbers become the same.

Important Expression:
---------------------
right & (right - 1)
    → Removes the lowest 1-bit.

Example:
    1100
    1011
    ----
    1000

Complexity:
-----------
Time:  O(number of bits) ≈ O(log n)
Space: O(1)

Memory Trick:
-------------
REMOVE RIGHTMOST 1 → UNTIL LEFT == RIGHT
"""

class Solution:
    def rangeBitwiseAnd(self, left, right):

        while right > left:              # Remove changing bits

            right = right & (right - 1)  # Remove the lowest set bit

        return right                     # Remaining common bits = answer
